 "pages": "p.3 (digital specs), p.4 (timing, pinout), p.5 (pin descriptions), p.15 (data format, VDRV)",
 "notModeled": [
  "analog inputs, references (INT/EXT internal/external reference select) and SEL input range select (2 V / 3 V): the result is always the 0 V (mid-scale) code 0x800 on both channels",
  "OEB: the clocked bus has one output enable, so OEA gates both the A1-A12 and B1-B12 outputs; OEB (pin 6) is not modeled",
  "OVRA/OVRB over-range outputs are never driven (a 0 V input is in range: they would be low)",
  "pipeline latency of 6 clock cycles (the code is constant)",
  "data valid DVA/DVB: modeled as the inverted CLK delayed tOut; the datasheet gives DV edges 7.5/5.6 ns typical (t3/t4) after the clock and a data valid window",
  "clock period limits (31.25 ns / 20 ns min, 100 us max)",
  "vcc is the VDRV output driver range (+2.7 V to +5 V, p.4 note 1); CLK, OE and SEL inputs are +3 V/+5 V CMOS compatible (VIH 2.4 V, high-level input current specified at VIN = 5 V), so inputMax is the +VS maximum 5.25 V"
 ],
